@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - UC-11 - Configure Application Settings

autonumber
actor Learner
participant "Desktop UI" as UI
participant "SettingsController" as Controller
participant "UpdateApplicationSettingsUseCase" as UseCase
participant "AppSettingsRepository" as Repo
participant "AppSettings" as Settings
participant "SettingsMapper" as Mapper

Learner -> UI : edit theme, notifications or retention
UI -> Controller : PUT /api/v1/settings/application\n{theme, notifications, retentionDays}
Controller -> UseCase : update(command)
UseCase -> UseCase : validate(command)

UseCase -> Repo : load()
Repo --> UseCase : AppSettings
UseCase -> Settings : updateTheme(theme)
UseCase -> Settings : updateNotifications(notifications)
UseCase -> Settings : updatePrivacy(retention)
Settings --> UseCase : updated
UseCase -> Repo : save(settings)
Repo --> UseCase : saved
UseCase -> Mapper : toDto(settings)
Mapper --> UseCase : SettingsDto
UseCase --> Controller : SettingsDto
Controller --> UI : 200 OK\n{...}

note over UseCase
  Data erasure is a separate confirmed command:
  it delegates to a maintenance port, deletes
  sessions, intervals, distraction logs,
  progress and settings, then recreates defaults.
end note

note over Settings
  Settings changes apply to new sessions.
  The active session keeps its snapshotted settings.
end note

@enduml
